#
# vLLM 0.32.0 declares requires-python >=3.11 (pyproject.toml:34), but the
# floor is a by-product of an import cleanup, not a runtime dependency: 0.32
# moved five names (Self / Never / Required / NotRequired / assert_never) from
# typing_extensions back to typing, and those only exist in typing from 3.11.
# Same five names, by source:  0.24.0 typing=0 / typing_extensions=28 files;
# 0.28.0 typing=0 / typing_extensions=32; 0.32.0 typing=37 / typing_extensions=0.
# 37 files carry the five names; 2 more carry datetime.UTC. Total 39.
#
# Zero 3.11-only runtime features are used (no ExceptionGroup / except* /
# TaskGroup / tomllib / StrEnum / PEP 695 generics); the single sys.version_info
# gate (distributed/utils.py:41, USE_SCHED_YIELD) already falls back to
# time.sleep(0). typing_extensions >= 4.10 is already in
# requirements/common.txt:30 and carries all five names.
#
# This patch makes the tree importable and servable on Python 3.10. Scope is
# vllm/ only: tests/ and tools/ are not shipped in the wheel, so leaving them
# alone keeps the patch surface minimal. Verified on py3.10 (torch 2.8.0 /
# 2.9.0 / 2.11.0): import vllm, vllm.v1.engine.core.EngineCore and
# vllm.entrypoints.openai.api_server all import clean.
#
# Registered but NOT enabled: this lives in patches/proposed/, which
# build-and-repack.sh's `"$SCRIPT_DIR"/patches/*.patch` glob does not reach, so
# today's wheels are unaffected. Promote it to patches/ when a py3.10 backend
# is actually attempted.
#
# Rebase on every vLLM bump, in the same pass as
# 0001-parallel-state-symm-mem-guard.patch. Generic hunks (diff -u from the
# pristine tarball), so a failed hunk means the source drifted — fail loudly.
#
# requires-python itself is NOT relaxed here on purpose: pip enforces
# Requires-Python at metadata time, so a py3.10 backend also needs either
# `--ignore-requires-python` at install or a relaxed declaration. That is a
# one-line edit to pyproject.toml plus a repack-side Requires-Python rewrite,
# decided when the first py3.10 backend is actually attempted — see
# packaging/vllm/docs/vllm-0.32.0-torch-floor.html §6.1.
